# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RHRMS — what does not belong in version control
#
# Two rules behind this list:
#   - generated things are not committed, because they go stale and conflict on
#     every merge while adding nothing a rebuild would not give you
#   - anything that could hold a real password is not committed, even when the
#     copy on this machine only holds a development one
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- Maven build output ---------------------------------------------------
# app/target/ holds the compiled classes, rhrms.jar and the seven dependency
# jars copied next to it: roughly 3.5 MB, all of it rebuilt by
# ./scripts/build_app.sh in a few seconds. This is 85 of the files git would
# otherwise stage today.
target/

# ---- real configuration, as opposed to the template ----------------------
# AppConfig looks for rhrms.properties in the working directory, then the
# parent, then app/, before falling back to the copy inside the jar. Those
# first paths are where a real front-desk install puts its own file, with the
# rescue's actual database passwords in it.
#
# The template at app/src/main/resources/rhrms.properties IS committed — it
# carries the documented development passwords and is the thing you copy and
# edit. These three entries cover the copies, not the template.
/rhrms.properties
/app/rhrms.properties
/app/target/rhrms.properties

# ---- PostgreSQL credentials ----------------------------------------------
# setup_db.sh writes the role passwords to $PGPASSFILE, which defaults to
# ~/.pgpass, outside this repository. These entries exist for the case where
# somebody points PGPASSFILE at a path inside it.
.pgpass
*.pgpass

# ---- runtime state and logs ----------------------------------------------
# The server's pid and log live in app/target/ (already covered above), but
# Crash.java falls back to the working directory when it cannot write beside
# the jar, so rhrms-terminal.log can appear at the repository root.
*.log
rhrms-server.pid

# ---- generated from the spreadsheet --------------------------------------
# scripts/import/read_master.py writes this from
# Documents/MASTER copy FINAL (2).xlsx. Both the script and the spreadsheet are
# committed, so the transcription is reproducible and does not need to be.
/scripts/import/master_verbatim.sql

# ---- editors and IDEs -----------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# ---- operating systems ----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
